      {
        "id": 51768,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T14:26:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I played Gloomy a little while ago, and tried using the 3 cultists to relic rule, and having him flip as soon as two relics are in play.</p><p>Much better rate of flipping with those two changes.</p><p>We also tried having three cultists summon a relic, but only destroying one cultist. &nbsp;That really caused him to flip, without the difficulty dip from the rule clearing all those cultists for you. We originally tried this alteration as a thematic change, a human sacrifice ritual instead of a suicide cult ritual, but I liked the way it changed the game.</p><p>I played around with having the relic summon when there are 6-(H) cultists, and killing one, since with 5 heroes it is nearly impossible for gloomy to keep cultists alive. &nbsp;Still not hard to ruin the fight with Omnitron-X or Adept, but other than them it is a pretty decent fight.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:25:29.240Z",
