      {
        "id": 51769,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-04T14:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I played Gloomy a little while ago, and tried using the 3 cultists to relic rule, and having him flip as soon as two relics are in play.Much better rate of flipping with those two changes.We also tried having three cultists summon a relic, but only destroying one cultist. &nbsp;That really caused him to flip, without the difficulty dip from the rule clearing all those cultists for you. We originally tried this alteration as a thematic change, a human sacrifice ritual instead of a suicide cult ritual, but I liked the way it changed the game.I played around with having the relic summon when there are 6-(H) cultists, and killing one, since with 5 heroes it is nearly impossible for gloomy to keep cultists alive. &nbsp;Still not hard to ruin the fight with Omnitron-X or Adept, but other than them it is a pretty decent fight.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I also like to start the game with the Zombie Ongoing card in play. The initial zombie attacks are pretty heafty that way and really put a clock on the game. Having a Relic on the bottom of his deck is a pain in the arse since it drags the game out and eventually you will lose that damage battle of attrition.</p>\n<p>Edit: I wonder if Gloomweaver will see any changes in the reprint of Infernal Relics? Surely the &gt;G guys know in their hearts that Gloomy is&nbsp;<em>not</em> a lvl3 difficulty villain in his current iteration. Might we see a slight change? A fan can hope.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:25:29.312Z",
